-- title:
--   Burnside span for ρ from a companion representation
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$, a non-zero $N$, and a finite set $S$ of naturals containing every prime divisor of $N$. Let $\mathcal{O}'$ be a discrete valuation domain with fraction field $K$, let $\chi$ be a ring homomorphism from [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra N 2 S`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18) — the $\mathbb{Z}$-subalgebra of $\operatorname{End}_{\mathbb{C}} S_2(\Gamma_0(N))$ generated by the operators $T_\ell$ for primes $\ell \nmid N$, $\ell \notin S$ and $U_q$ for primes $q \mid N$, $q \notin S$ — to $\mathcal{O}'$, and let $\rho$ be a [`GaloisRepAdic`](def/GaloisRep_Adic.html#L16) over $\mathcal{O}'$: a free $\mathcal{O}'$-module $V$ of rank $2$ with an adically continuous monoid homomorphism $\rho$ from $\operatorname{Gal}(\bar{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q})$ to $\operatorname{End}_{\mathcal{O}'}V$. Assume that for every prime $\ell \nmid N$ with $\ell \notin S$, every valuation subring $A$ of $\bar{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $\ell$ a non-unit of $A$ and every $\sigma$ lying in the decomposition group of $A$ and acting as $x \mapsto x^{\ell}$ on its residue field, $\operatorname{charpoly}(\rho(\sigma)) = X^2 - \chi(T_\ell)X + \ell$. Let further $\mathcal{O}''$ be a complete discrete valuation domain of characteristic zero with finite residue field, $\varphi : \mathcal{O}' \to \mathcal{O}''$ a local homomorphism, $K''$ the fraction field of $\mathcal{O}''$, made a $K$- and $\mathcal{O}'$-algebra compatibly with $\varphi$ (so $\operatorname{algebraMap}_{\mathcal{O}' \to K''} = \operatorname{algebraMap}_{\mathcal{O}'' \to K''} \circ \varphi$), and let $\rho\chi$ be a [`GaloisRepAdic`](def/GaloisRep_Adic.html#L16) over $\mathcal{O}''$ with $p$ in the maximal ideal of $\mathcal{O}''$ such that: $\rho\chi$ is unramified at every prime $q \nmid N$, $q \neq p$, meaning that every element of the inertia subgroup of every valuation subring of $\bar{\mathbb{Q}}$ in which $q$ is a non-unit acts as the identity; for every finite extension field $L$ of $K''$ carrying compatible $\mathcal{O}''$- and $K''$-algebra structures and every $L$-line $W \subseteq L \otimes_{\mathcal{O}''} \rho\chi.V$ stable under all base-changed operators $(\rho\chi(\sigma))_L$, either some positive power $n$ satisfies $((\rho\chi(\sigma))_L)^n w = w$ for all $w \in W$ and all $\sigma$ in the inertia group of any valuation subring in which $p$ is a non-unit, or some positive power $n$ satisfies $((\rho\chi(\sigma))_L)^n v - v \in W$ for all $v$ and all such $\sigma$; and the Frobenius characteristic polynomials of $\rho\chi$ at primes $\ell \nmid N$, $\ell \notin S$ are $X^2 - \varphi(\chi(T_\ell))X + \ell$. The conclusion is that the $K$-span of the set of base-changed endomorphisms $(\rho(\sigma))_K$ on $K \otimes_{\mathcal{O}'} V$, as $\sigma$ ranges over $\operatorname{Gal}(\bar{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q})$, is everything.
--
--   By Burnside's theorem the stated spanning condition is the absolute irreducibility of the two-dimensional $K$-representation obtained from $\rho$ by base change; the companion representation $\rho\chi$ over a complete coefficient ring, with the same Frobenius characteristic polynomials and the local dichotomy at $p$, is what transports Ribet's irreducibility argument to $\rho$. It is used by [`RibetIrr.irreducible_of_point_of_not_dvd`](thm.html#RibetIrr.irreducible_of_point_of_not_dvd).
